      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems complicated to implement and prone to race conditions.\n\nAlso - will existing users of onClientsChanged expect to see local-only clients in the callback? If not, then I guess they could get confused, and assume that all local-only clients are actually tethered clients.\n\nCan we do better than this? If currently onClientsChanged *only* reports tethered devices (not local-only), then we should add a new onLocalOnlyClientsChanged that reports only local-only clients.\n\nIf onClientsChanged currently reports results for local-only clients as well, then we should at least add something to TetheredClient or to onClientsChanged that allows the caller to know where this client is. Maybe we could add a TetheringInterface member to TetheredClient?",
